      "message": "**Location:** `util/egis/bootrom.cc`\n\n**The Problem:** In `SystemReset()`, you append `0x01` to the command without explanation. In `SendBootromCommandAes()`, you hardcode the Additional Authenticated Data (AAD): `uint8_t aad[4] \u003d {0x01, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00};`\n\n**The Fix:** Declare these values as named constants in `bootrom.h` to explain their intent.\n\n*In `bootrom.h`:*\n\n```c\nnamespace EgisBootrom {\n  // ...\n  constexpr uint8_t kSystemResetTypeNormal \u003d 0x01;\n  \n  // Chip ID / Revision used as AAD for AES-GCM\n  constexpr uint32_t kChipIdAad \u003d 0x00000001; \n}\n\n```\n\n*In `bootrom.cc` (`SystemReset`):*\n\n```c\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e cmd \u003d {EgisBootrom::kCmdSystemReset, \n                              EgisBootrom::kSystemResetTypeNormal};\n\n```\n\n*In `bootrom.cc` (`SendBootromCommandAes`):*\n\n```c\n  // Use your AppendLittleEndian helper to convert the uint32_t into a byte array dynamically\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e aad_vec;\n  AppendLittleEndian(aad_vec, EgisBootrom::kChipIdAad);\n  \n  if (!AesGcmEncryptOpenssl(aes_key_, header.iv, aad_vec, data, ciphertext, header.tag)) { ... }\n\n```",
