      "writtenOn": "2026-05-22T17:44:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are multiple places in the code that manually check `if constexpr (std::endian::native !\u003d std::endian::little)` and apply `std::byteswap`. This is repetitive and error-prone. Creating generic `ToLittleEndian` and `FromLittleEndian` templates centralizes this logic, significantly reducing boilerplate and making struct assignments cleaner.\n\n### Detailed Fix\n\n**Location:** `util/egis/egis_util.h`\n\nAdd the templates and refactor the existing `AppendLittleEndian` and `ReadLittleEndian` to use them.\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nconstexpr T ToLittleEndian(T value) {\n  return (std::endian::native \u003d\u003d std::endian::little) ? value : std::byteswap(value);\n}\n\n// Semantic alias for reading\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nconstexpr T FromLittleEndian(T value) {\n  return ToLittleEndian(value);\n}\n\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nvoid AppendLittleEndian(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e \u0026vec, T value) {\n  T le_value \u003d ToLittleEndian(value);\n  const auto *bytes \u003d reinterpret_cast\u003cconst uint8_t *\u003e(\u0026le_value);\n  vec.append_range(std::span(bytes, sizeof(T)));\n}\n\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cT, int\u003e ReadLittleEndian(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buffer) {\n  if (buffer.size() \u003c sizeof(T)) return std::unexpected(-1);\n  T value;\n  std::memcpy(\u0026value, buffer.data(), sizeof(T));\n  return FromLittleEndian(value);\n}\n\n```\n\n*(Once added, replace manual byte-swapping blocks in `ec_comm.cc` and `bootrom.cc` with inline calls to `ToLittleEndian()`.)*",
